# long64.rc with Zend's memory manager switched back ON, and nothing else changed.
#
# PENDING because nothing here has been built. It needs src/patch-zend-alloc.sh
# to find the upstream setting first, and that script fails loudly rather than
# guessing -- rename to zendalloc.rc once it links.
#
# MEASURED ON THE SHIPPING BUILD, not inferred: PHP answers
# getenv('USE_ZEND_ALLOC') === '0', so every emalloc goes straight to the system
# allocator and zend_mm is out of the loop entirely. The string USE_ZEND_ALLOC=0
# is in the .wasm data section, so it comes from upstream php-wasm rather than
# from any rc in this repository. Zend's manager wants 2 MiB-aligned chunks from
# mmap, which emscripten emulates poorly, so the default is defensible -- it has
# simply never been re-scored.
#
# THREE THINGS ARE OFF BECAUSE OF THAT ONE FLAG, and each was recorded elsewhere
# as its own unexplained platform quirk:
#
#   - memory_get_usage() reads 0, which is the "build property" the consumer's
#     RULE 0 names. The counter lives in zend_mm and nothing increments it.
#   - memory_limit IS NOT ENFORCED. The check is in the same allocator. An 8M cap
#     holds 38 MB of strings with no error; the consumer asserts this.
#   - the cycle collector never runs: gc_status() reports runs 0, collected 0.
#
# THE PRIZE IS AVAILABILITY, NOT SPEED, and that is what makes it worth an arm.
# Today a runaway allocation does not stop at a catchable PHP fatal that loses one
# request. It grows linear memory until workerd's 128 MiB ceiling refuses, and
# emscripten turns that into exit(1) with nothing on stderr, which loses the whole
# object and every session on it.
#
# SCORE IT ON: whether memory_limit actually stops an over-allocation, whether
# memory_get_usage becomes non-zero, and then peak heap for the AUTHENTICATED
# render -- which is the binding workload and where the consumer's margin is
# 19.50 MiB. Zend's 2 MiB chunk granularity could spend that margin, so a higher
# peak is the way this arm loses and it must be measured before anything ships.
#
# NOT A RUNTIME LEVER, unlike the growth step. Module.ENV is applied by the glue in
# a preRun hook, but a probe variable set that way does not reach PHP's getenv at
# all -- so either php-wasm drops the key or the C overwrites it, and which of the
# two is UNDETERMINED. Do not write it down as settled without measuring it.

# ZEND_ALLOC=1
# the shipping ABI, held constant so this arm has exactly one variable against what
# ships; without it the arm would silently be a wasm32 comparison
# ZEND_LONG64=1

PHP_VERSION=8.5

MAIN_MODULE=0
ASYNCIFY=0
OPTIMIZE=2
INITIAL_MEMORY=96MB

WITH_VRZNO=1
WITH_LIBXML=static
WITH_DOM=static
WITH_SIMPLEXML=static
WITH_XML=static
WITH_YAML=static
WITH_ZLIB=static

WITH_CTYPE=1
WITH_FILTER=1
WITH_SESSION=1
WITH_TOKENIZER=1

WITH_BCMATH=0
WITH_CALENDAR=0
WITH_EXIF=0

WITH_ICONV=0
WITH_MBSTRING=0
WITH_ONIGURUMA=0
WITH_SQLITE=0
WITH_GD=0
WITH_LIBPNG=0
WITH_LIBJPEG=0
WITH_FREETYPE=0
WITH_LIBWEBP=0
WITH_LIBZIP=0
WITH_PHAR=0
WITH_XMLREADER=0
WITH_XMLWRITER=0
WITH_INTL=0
WITH_TIDY=0
WITH_SDL=0
WITH_OPENSSL=0
WITH_PDO_PGLITE=0
WITH_PDO_CFD1=0
WITH_WAITLINE=0

# opcache is compiled in; file_cache_only is set at runtime from the worker ini
CONFIGURE_FLAGS+= --enable-opcache
